    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds. Let me summarize what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nI introduced address normalization applied when an owner is created, satisfying the spec and all tests (3/3 acceptance tests green, `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n### Changes\n\n**`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a canonical, reusable address normalizer and routed household comparisons through it:\n- New `public static String normalizeAddress(String)`: trims and collapses whitespace, upper-cases, and expands whole-word abbreviations (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). Returns `\"\"` for null/blank input, and is idempotent.\n- `sameHouseholdAs(...)` and `householdKey()` now compare the **address** via `normalizeAddress(...)` instead of the old lowercase-collapse `normalize(...)`. The last-name comparison keeps the existing case/whitespace folding. (I preserved the existing NUL byte separator in `householdKey`, which the Read tool renders as a space.)\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 `normalizeNewOwner(...)` (already the single place field normalization happens before household comparisons) now:\n- Normalizes the address first via `Owner.normalizeAddress(...)`, storing the canonical form (so it's what gets persisted and returned).\n- Rejects the create with `400 Bad Request` when the address is blank after normalization.\n\nBecause normalization runs before `findHouseholdMember` / `joinHousehold`, both duplicate detection and the derived shared household id operate on the normalized address, as required.\n\n### Verification against the tests\n- `\"  12  main  st \"` \u2192 `\"12 MAIN STREET\"` \u2713\n- `\"7 elm ave\"` \u2192 `\"7 ELM AVENUE\"` \u2713\n- `\"   \"` \u2192 rejected with 400 \u2713\n\nI left the `updateOwner` path untouched since the spec scopes this to owner **creation**.",
